## 2. An injected inline script (stored XSS in the employer notice)
   concept: both builds render the notice unescaped; on the hardened one CSP refuses any inline script without this response's nonce and reports the violation
   [insecure :53052] signed in Alice Martin
   [attacker :53252] received document.cookie "session=adW-nhkZJuRJ4Dc_3OJM_k44" from http://localhost:53052/
   [attacker :53252] received document.cookie "session=adW-nhkZJuRJ4Dc_3OJM_k44" from http://localhost:53052/
   insecure: injected script ran: YES; page scripts: "inline script ran", "widget.js loaded by the inline script (strict-dynamic)"; document.cookie visible to scripts: "session=..."
   [hardened :53152] signed in Alice Martin
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: script-src-elem blocked inline on http://localhost:53152/ sample "document.getElementById('notice').insert"
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: script-src-elem blocked inline on http://localhost:53152/ sample "document.getElementById('notice').insert"
   hardened: injected script ran: no; page scripts: "inline script ran (it carries the nonce)", "widget.js loaded by the inline script (strict-dynamic)"; document.cookie visible to scripts: ""
   hardened console: Refused to execute inline script because it violates the following Content Security Policy directive: "script-src 'nonce-<random>' 'strict-dynamic' 'report-sample'". Either the 'unsafe-inline' keyword, a hash ('sha256-Xt7ETpeWQx3p
   ok: insecure: the injected script ran and sent the session cookie to the attacker
   ok: hardened: the injected script did not run and the attacker received nothing
   ok: hardened: the page's own nonce'd script ran and the script it loaded ran too (strict-dynamic)
   ok: hardened: the browser sent a CSP report naming the blocked inline script
   ok: the hardened session cookie is HttpOnly: invisible to scripts even if one ran

## 3. A cross-origin form post (CSRF)
   concept: the attacker's page auto-submits a form to /bank; the browser attaches the portal's cookie; the hardened portal checks Origin and a CSRF token bound to the session
   [insecure :53052] signed in Alice Martin
   [attacker :53252] received document.cookie "session=c5dsItT_9trlVnZwUjMYuEE4" from http://localhost:53052/
   [insecure :53052] bank details changed to "XX00 ATTACKER 0000 0000" (Origin http://localhost:53252)
   insecure: POST /bank from http://localhost:53252 -> 200; IBAN before "FR76 3000 6000 0112 3456 7890 189", after "XX00 ATTACKER 0000 0000"
   [hardened :53152] signed in Alice Martin
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: script-src-elem blocked inline on http://localhost:53152/ sample "document.getElementById('notice').insert"
   [hardened :53152] 403 POST /bank: cross-origin request (Origin http://localhost:53252), session cookie present
   hardened: POST /bank from http://localhost:53252 -> 403; IBAN before "FR76 3000 6000 0112 3456 7890 189", after "FR76 3000 6000 0112 3456 7890 189"
   ok: insecure: the forged post changed the bank details to the attacker's IBAN
   ok: hardened: the forged post was rejected (403) and the IBAN is unchanged
   ok: same site, other origin: SameSite=Lax still sent the cookie; the Origin check stopped it
   [hardened :53152] signed in Alice Martin
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: script-src-elem blocked inline on http://localhost:53152/ sample "document.getElementById('notice').insert"
   [hardened :53152] 403 POST /bank: cross-origin request (Origin http://127.0.0.1:53252), session cookie absent
   hardened: POST /bank from http://127.0.0.1:53252 (another site) -> 403
   ok: cross-site: SameSite=Lax kept the session cookie off the forged POST
   [hardened :53152] signed in Scanner
   [hardened :53152] 403 POST /bank: missing or wrong CSRF token (http://localhost:53152)
   hardened: POST /bank with a valid session and a matching Origin but no CSRF token -> 403
   ok: hardened: without the CSRF token the post is refused even when the Origin matches
   [hardened :53152] signed in Alice Martin
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: script-src-elem blocked inline on http://localhost:53152/ sample "document.getElementById('notice').insert"
   [hardened :53152] bank details changed to "FR76 1027 8060 4100 0202 0870 165" (Origin http://localhost:53152)
   hardened: the member's own form (same origin, with the token) -> changed, IBAN now "FR76 1027 8060 4100 0202 0870 165"
   ok: hardened: the legitimate form post with its CSRF token still works

## 4. Framing (clickjacking)
   concept: the attacker page loads the portal in a transparent iframe over a fake button; frame-ancestors 'none' (and X-Frame-Options: DENY) make the browser refuse to render it
   [insecure :53052] signed in Alice Martin
   [attacker :53252] received document.cookie "session=kLH495uyIGlKe0z0uhLn3-Fq" from http://localhost:53052/
   [attacker :53252] received document.cookie "session=kLH495uyIGlKe0z0uhLn3-Fq" from http://localhost:53052/
   insecure: iframe rendered the portal ("Welcome, Alice Martin")
   [hardened :53152] signed in Alice Martin
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: script-src-elem blocked inline on http://localhost:53152/ sample "document.getElementById('notice').insert"
   [hardened :53152] CSP report: frame-ancestors blocked http://localhost:53152/ on http://localhost:53152/
   hardened: iframe blocked (frame url chrome-error://chromewebdata/)
   ok: the insecure portal renders inside the attacker's page; the hardened one does not
   ok: hardened: the browser reported the frame-ancestors violation

