## 6. Secrets: from the environment, rotated with a key ring
   concept: SESSION_KEYS='new,old': the first key signs, all keys verify; rotation is add-new, wait out the sessions, drop-old
   cookie signed with k1: verifies under "k2,k1": yes; under "k2" alone: no; a new cookie signed under "k2,k1" verifies under "k2": yes
   ok: rotation: old cookies stay valid while both keys are loaded and stop working once the old key is dropped
   gitleaks, working tree: 2 finding(s)
      generic-api-key in .env.local
      npm-access-token in .env.local
   gitleaks, files git would commit: 0 finding(s); .env.local ignored by git: yes
   ok: the secret scanner finds the local .env.local, which git ignores; nothing secret is committable

